-- ============================================================
-- Against the Odds: wiring
-- ============================================================
--
-- TODO.md: "Pathfinding (Renamed to Against the odds) (0, 2): Your multi-shot
-- has a 50/100% chance to also cast an empowered Beast Cleave when it hits an
-- enemy, dealing 100% more damage. (2 ranks)"
--
-- All three retail effects go: an aspect-speed modifier and the mounted/flight
-- speed auras.
--
-- The empowerment is a MARKER (200749), not a second "empowered Beast Cleave"
-- spell.  A parallel aura would put two Beast Cleave instances on the pet, both
-- of which pass spell_hun_beast_cleave's CheckProc, and every pet swing would
-- splash twice.  One aura plus a marker the splash reads is the only shape that
-- cannot double-fire.  It also means a manually-cast Beast Cleave inside the
-- window is empowered too, which is the intended feel.
--
-- Both effects are SPELL_AURA_PROC_TRIGGER_SPELL on the same aura and both fire
-- on the same proc -- Aura::TriggerProcOnEvent walks every proc-capable effect.
-- So this needs no C++ at all on the trigger side; the only code change is the
-- three lines in HunterBeastCleave.cpp that read 200749.
--
-- 13161 already targets TARGET_UNIT_PET, so it lands on the pet with no extra
-- plumbing.  200749 is given the SAME implicit target (5) for the same reason:
-- with target 1 it would apply to the hunter, where nothing reads it.
--
-- The triggered 13161 does NOT touch the player's own Beast Cleave cooldown.
-- AuraEffect::HandleProcTriggerSpellAuraProc (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:6914) casts
-- with triggered = true, which is TRIGGERED_FULL_MASK, and
-- Spell::SendSpellCooldown (Spell.cpp:4356) returns early on
-- TRIGGERED_IGNORE_SPELL_AND_CATEGORY_CD -- so the cooldown is neither consumed
-- nor set.
--
-- 200749's DurationIndex is 8 (15s), matching 13161's retuned window, NOT 35
-- (4s).  Beast Cleave was retuned from 4s/6s to 15s/30s in woa_2026_08_11_00.sql
-- and a 4s marker would leave the last 11 seconds unempowered.
--
-- SpellFamilyMask0 4096 is the Multi-Shot chain (2643/14288/14289/14290/25294/
-- 27021/49047/49048), family 9.  ProcFlags 0x100 is
-- PROC_FLAG_DONE_SPELL_RANGED_DMG_CLASS.  Two rows because the chance differs
-- per rank and spell_proc is keyed by spell id.
--
-- AttributesMask stays 0: Multi-Shot is a real player cast, not a triggered
-- child.
DELETE FROM `spell_proc` WHERE `SpellId` IN (19559, 19560);
INSERT INTO `spell_proc` (`SpellId`, `SchoolMask`, `SpellFamilyName`, `SpellFamilyMask0`, `SpellFamilyMask1`, `SpellFamilyMask2`, `ProcFlags`, `SpellTypeMask`, `SpellPhaseMask`, `HitMask`, `AttributesMask`, `DisableEffectsMask`, `ProcsPerMinute`, `Chance`, `Cooldown`, `Charges`) VALUES
(19559, 0, 9, 4096, 0, 0, 256, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 50, 0, 0),
(19560, 0, 9, 4096, 0, 0, 256, 0, 2, 0, 0, 0, 0, 100, 0, 0);
